cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these results, please cite them as below."
title: "Code and results for: Noise-Robust Multi-Objective Feature Selection with Leakage Testing for Intrusion Detection in Internet of Medical Things Networks"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Alozie
    given-names: Chisom Elizabeth
    affiliation: "University of the Cumberlands"
  - family-names: Adieze
    given-names: Chidinma Queen
    affiliation: "Western Governors University"
  - family-names: Emesiani
    given-names: Fabian
    affiliation: "Westcliff University"
version: "1.0.1"
date-released: "2026-11-15"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Chisom303/Feature-selection-codes"
abstract: >-
  Jupyter notebooks and run-level results for a three-objective NSGA-II feature
  selection study with archive consensus on eight CICIoMT2024 traffic classes,
  including robustness tests under synthetic and group-correlated noise, a
  meaning-based noise-mask search, stability analysis, and leakage tests of the
  inter-arrival time (IAT) feature. The CICIoMT2024 data are not redistributed.
keywords:
  - IoMT security
  - intrusion detection
  - multi-objective feature selection
  - NSGA-II
  - data leakage
  - robustness
  - CICIoMT2024
